# WARPAZ TCG

Stack: Unity **6000.3.20f1** + C#. Do not upgrade the editor without a new ADR.

## Layers

- **Domain**: pure C#. No `UnityEngine`, scenes, GameObjects, animation, or input.
- **Application**: use cases (session, replay, bot). No visual decisions.
- **Content**: card definitions, `RuleConfig`, importers, validators.
- **Infrastructure**: JSON/CSV, filesystem, logs, paths.
- **Presentation**: scenes, MonoBehaviours, UI, animation. Renders `GameState` and sends `Command`s.

```csharp
// BAD — UI decides legality
if (card.CostPa <= player.Pa) Play(card);

// GOOD — engine decides; UI only submits
session.Submit(Command.Play(actorId, state.EventIndex, instanceId));
```

## State

- Mutate state only through `Command`s. Observable results only through `GameEvent`s.
- UI never decides if an action is legal. Rejected commands must not mutate `GameState`.
- No randomness without a recorded seed. No `UnityEngine.Random` in Domain.

## Cards

- Identify cards only by `cardId`. Names are never keys.
- WZ1-001 … WZ1-120 are immutable. Effects are declarative and reusable.
- Exception handlers register by `cardId`. Never one MonoBehaviour per card.

## Out of scope

No Locations, Missions, backend, network, accounts, or economy. Dice exist only as an explicit card effect.

## Quality

Every feature needs tests. Do not ignore compile errors. Do not start the next slice while the console has red errors.
